TST-001 · Scenario

190
00:10:58,215 --> 00:11:02,292
Product teams also test their own screens that contain ui-tabs.

191
00:11:02,292 --> 00:11:07,185
Their tests query .ui-tabs__tab--active and broke when the library renamed that class.

192
00:11:08,559 --> 00:11:10,227
TST-001 · Interview question

193
00:11:11,352 --> 00:11:13,592
Why did these tests not catch the bugs?

194
00:11:13,592 --> 00:11:15,551
Rewrite the testing approach for the library,

195
00:11:15,551 --> 00:11:18,350
and say what the library should give product teams for

196
00:11:18,350 --> 00:11:18,910
their tests.

197
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:28,695
TST-001 · Why they missed everything

198
00:11:29,821 --> 00:11:30,630
No content.

199
00:11:30,630 --> 00:11:35,486
TestBed.createComponent(TabsComponent) renders the tabs with nothing projected, so there are no tabs.

200
00:11:35,486 --> 00:11:38,723
Someone made the test pass by asserting toBeNull(),

201
00:11:38,723 --> 00:11:41,961
so it now checks that nothing is selected,

202
00:11:41,961 --> 00:11:43,175
which is meaningless.

203
00:11:43,175 --> 00:11:43,984
Driving internals.

204
00:11:43,984 --> 00:11:47,222
Calling select(1) skips what users actually do (click,

205
00:11:47,222 --> 00:11:50,864
arrow keys, Home, End), so keyboard support was never

206
00:11:50,864 --> 00:11:51,269
exercised.

207
00:11:51,269 --> 00:11:54,911
Asserting on private markup. .ui-tabs__tab--active is an internal class.

208
00:11:54,911 --> 00:12:00,576
The tests say nothing about what users and assistive technology perceive: roles, aria-selected, focus.

209
00:12:00,576 --> 00:12:05,028
Testing that a method exists checks the TypeScript compiler, not behaviour.

210
00:12:05,028 --> 00:12:06,242
One instance only.

211
00:12:06,242 --> 00:12:10,288
The duplicate-id bug needs two tab groups on one page.

212
00:12:11,664 --> 00:12:15,944
TST-001 · The approach: test through a host, like a consumer

213
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:21,348
Render the component inside a small host component whose template looks like real

214
00:12:21,348 --> 00:12:25,628
usage, interact the way users do, and assert on roles, states and focus.

