275
00:15:54,404 --> 00:15:58,453
TST-001 · Ship a harness: the library's testing API

276
00:15:59,578 --> 00:16:03,983
The harness is published from a testing entry point (@acme/ui/tabs/testing), documented,

277
00:16:03,983 --> 00:16:07,989
and covered by the same versioning rules as the component.

278
00:16:09,364 --> 00:16:13,481
TST-001 · What else belongs in the library's test strategy

279
00:16:14,606 --> 00:16:17,548
Accessibility checks with axe on every component state.

280
00:16:17,548 --> 00:16:21,595
Run them in a real browser (for example Vitest browser mode

281
00:16:21,595 --> 00:16:25,642
or Playwright), because DOM emulations cannot compute colour contrast or layout.

282
00:16:25,642 --> 00:16:30,792
Visual regression tests for each component in each theme, so token changes are reviewed.

283
00:16:30,792 --> 00:16:35,574
Keyboard tests written from the ARIA pattern's keyboard table, one assertion per row.

284
00:16:35,574 --> 00:16:39,989
Forms tests with a real FormControl for every form control (see API-004).

285
00:16:41,364 --> 00:16:43,488
TST-001 · Follow-up 1

286
00:16:44,613 --> 00:16:49,815
What belongs in a harness's API, and what should never be exposed?

287
00:16:55,087 --> 00:16:59,185
Expose task-level operations and observable state: select a tab by label,

288
00:16:59,185 --> 00:17:02,166
read the selected label, send a supported key,

289
00:17:02,166 --> 00:17:04,774
and inspect focus when that is meaningful.

290
00:17:04,774 --> 00:17:08,873
Hide private fields, raw nodes, styling classes, and internal component hierarchy.

291
00:17:08,873 --> 00:17:13,344
The harness can use internal selectors because the library owns their maintenance.

292
00:17:13,344 --> 00:17:17,070
Publish filters and useful errors, and version the harness API.

293
00:17:17,070 --> 00:17:20,424
If consumers still need to query private DOM after

294
00:17:20,424 --> 00:17:23,405
obtaining the harness, revisit the missing supported operation.

295
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:26,877
TST-001 · Follow-up 2

296
00:17:28,002 --> 00:17:31,671
How would you test that a live region announcement happens?

297
00:17:37,021 --> 00:17:42,047
Verify a connected persistent live region receives the intended new text with the chosen

298
00:17:42,047 --> 00:17:46,714
politeness and timing, or verify the announcer boundary in a focused unit test.

299
00:17:46,714 --> 00:17:51,022
Then use real browser integration to ensure the region exists and updates.

300
00:17:51,022 --> 00:17:56,048
An automated DOM assertion cannot prove the exact speech emitted by a screen reader.

301
00:17:56,048 --> 00:17:59,279
Perform manual checks on supported combinations for repetition, interruption,

302
00:17:59,279 --> 00:18:02,869
and rapid changes, and record those limits in the test

303
00:18:02,869 --> 00:18:03,227
evidence.

304
00:18:04,603 --> 00:18:07,039
TST-001 · Follow-up 3

305
00:18:08,164 --> 00:18:12,469
Your visual regression suite has 2,000 screenshots and is flaky.

306
00:18:12,469 --> 00:18:14,192
What do you do?

307
00:18:19,366 --> 00:18:23,019
Classify flakes before changing thresholds: fonts, animation, data, timing,

308
00:18:23,019 --> 00:18:26,267
viewport, and actual layout races need different fixes.

309
00:18:26,267 --> 00:18:30,327
Freeze irrelevant variability and wait for a deterministic ready condition.

310
00:18:30,327 --> 00:18:34,386
Map each screenshot to a risk, keep representative themes and

311
00:18:34,386 --> 00:18:38,040
states, and remove redundant captures only when coverage remains.

312
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:39,664
Review baseline changes deliberately.

313
00:18:39,664 --> 00:18:43,724
Do not approve all two thousand images blindly or disable

314
00:18:43,724 --> 00:18:47,784
the suite; rebuild a smaller reliable signal with clear ownership.

315
00:18:49,159 --> 00:18:50,279
Final review checklist

316
00:18:51,404 --> 00:18:55,509
Review the lesson by answering each main question and follow-up aloud.

317
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:58,121
For Testing Angular Libraries Through Consumer Behavior,

318
00:18:58,121 --> 00:19:00,734
connect each reported symptom to its mechanism,

319
00:19:00,734 --> 00:19:04,466
explain the corrected public contract, and name a regression check

320
00:19:04,466 --> 00:19:06,332
that exercises the consumer path.

321
00:19:06,332 --> 00:19:08,571
State compatibility and accessibility limitations clearly.

322
00:19:08,571 --> 00:19:11,184
The linked transcript, complete code, source questions,

323
00:19:11,184 --> 00:19:14,916
and verification report let you repeat the exercises at your

324
00:19:14,916 --> 00:19:15,662
own pace.

325
00:19:16,705 --> 00:19:18,944
That's the end of lesson 6.

